  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between mitomycin and HEC-1 through a series of target interactions involving palmarumycin CP18. Mitomycin is linked to bromodomain-containing protein 4 and ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, both of which are targets of palmarumycin CP18, which in turn targets HEC-1. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent but moderate level of confidence in this relationship, likely due to the shared involvement of palmarumycin CP18 as a common mediator. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where mitomycin may influence HEC-1 through the activation or modulation of palmarumycin CP18, which could have downstream effects on cellular processes. The evidence supports a functional link between mitomycin and HEC-1, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
